window.AG_CHAPTERS["25"] = {"id":"25","title":"The Cold That Would Not End","titleZh":"過不完的冬","patient":{"name":"Uncle Cui the night watchman 守夜人崔伯","sprite":"man"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-treatment.jpg","key":"night"},"pattern":"Heart and Kidney Yang Deficiency 心腎陽虛","principle":"warm and supplement the yang of the Heart and Kidney, and move water by restoring qi transformation","tongue":"pale and swollen with tooth marks, coated white and visibly wet","pulseNote":{"en":"Deep, slow, and thin — you must press to the bone to find it at all.","zh":"脈沉、遲而細，重按至骨始得"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>T&#224;ix&#299; KI3</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"KI3","zh":"太谿","py":"T&#224;ix&#299;","x":113,"y":868,"img":"art/body-leg-medial.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":46,"y":756,"w":236,"h":290},"decoys":[{"x":102,"y":780},{"x":146,"y":890},{"x":113,"y":820},{"x":150,"y":852},{"x":90,"y":900}],"note":"<b>太谿 T&#224;ix&#299; KI3</b> — in the depression between the tip of the medial malleolus and the Achilles tendon, level with the tip of the malleolus. The Source point and the Stream point of the Kidney. You have needled it before for Kidney yin; today the same point is warmed for Kidney yang, and that is the lesson — a Source point supplements whichever half of its organ is short.<br>內踝尖與跟腱之間凹陷中，與內踝尖平齊。腎之原穴、輸穴。前此取之以滋腎陰，今則溫之以助腎陽——此正本章之旨：原穴所補者，隨其臟之所虧而異。"},"safety":{"ask":{"en":"Palpitations, swollen ankles and breathlessness in a man of sixty-one. Screen him before anything else.","zh":"六十一歲男子，心悸、足踝浮腫、氣促。此當先於一切而篩查。"},"lead":{"en":"This is the combination that must never be waved through. Three questions.","zh":"此組合斷不可輕放。當問三事。"},"opts":[{"t":"Ask whether he can lie flat, or whether he has to prop himself up to breathe at night","c":"問能否平臥，抑或夜須高枕方能息","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and it is the highest-value question in the whole case. Breathlessness that forces a patient to sit up at night is a serious sign and needs medical assessment the same week, not after a course of treatment. Uncle Cui sleeps flat and wakes only to relieve himself.<br><b>Safe to continue, and tell him plainly what would change that.</b><br>夜不得平臥而須端坐以息者，重候也，當於旬日內就醫，不可俟療程之畢。崔伯能平臥，夜起惟為小便。可續，且當明告其人：若不能平臥，即當就醫。"},{"t":"Ask whether the swelling pits when pressed, and whether it is in both legs equally","c":"問其腫按之凹陷否，兩足是否等大","ok":1,"note":"Correct. Symmetrical pitting swelling of both ankles that is worse by evening is one picture; sudden swelling of <i>one</i> leg with heat, redness and calf pain is an entirely different and urgent one, and it must be excluded by asking. His is both ankles, equal, worse in the evening, and neither leg is hot.<br><b>Safe to continue.</b><br>兩踝對稱而按之凹陷、日晡益甚者，一候也；若<b>一</b>腿驟腫、色赤而熱、腓腸疼痛，則為另一急候，必問而後可排除。今其人兩踝俱腫而等，暮則加重，兩腿俱不熱。可續。"},{"t":"Take the pulse specifically for pauses, and count them","c":"專察其脈有無歇止，並計其數","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and do it deliberately rather than in passing. A pulse that pauses — 結 irregular with pauses, 代 pausing at regular intervals and slow to resume — in a patient with palpitations and swelling is a finding to record, to count, and to re-check at every visit. His is slow and deep but regular today.<br><b>Safe to continue, and note the number so you can compare next week.</b><br>此當專察，不可順手帶過。心悸而兼浮腫，其脈見<b>結</b>（止無定數）或<b>代</b>（止有定數而還遲）者，當記其數，逐診比之。今其脈沉遲而不歇。可續，且宜記其至數，以備他日相較。"},{"t":"Skip the screening — the tongue is pale and swollen, so this is plainly yang deficiency","c":"不必篩查，舌淡胖，顯係陽虛","ok":0,"note":"It probably is yang deficiency. The screen is not asking what the pattern is; it is asking whether this patient can safely be treated only here, and a pale tongue answers neither question. In a case with palpitations, oedema and breathlessness, skipping the screen is the single most consequential shortcut available.<br>其證或誠屬陽虛。然篩查所問者非「何證」，乃「此人可否但治於此」；舌淡於二者皆無所答。心悸、浮腫、氣促並見者，省此一步，其失最重。"}]},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Ask what he does with his hands and feet at night, and what he drinks.","zh":"問其夜間手足何如，並問所飲。"},"look":{"en":"Look at the shape and the wet, not only the colour.","zh":"察其形與潤，勿獨察其色。"},"pulse":{"en":"Three qualities. One says where, one says how hot, one says how much.","zh":"三象並見：一言其位，一言其寒熱，一言其盈虛。"},"dx":{"en":"Two organs, one fire. Which one keeps the fire?","zh":"二臟一火。火藏於何？"},"rx":{"en":"Warm the root, not the branch. And do not forget the water.","zh":"當溫其本而非其標。且勿忘其水。"},"tech":{"en":"This is the case the moxa was made for.","zh":"艾灸之設，正為此案。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"patient","en":"Uncle Cui keeps his hands inside his sleeves the whole time, and the room is not cold.","zh":"崔伯自始至終袖手不出，而室中不寒。"},{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen takes one hand out of the sleeve, holds it, and says nothing for a while.","zh":"參師父自袖中取其一手，執之良久不語。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy looks at the old man&#39;s ankles above his shoes and glances at Master Shen.","zh":"藥童視其鞋上足踝，回望參師父一眼。"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"Spring came a month ago. I have not felt it. I am cold the way other men are cold in the twelfth month.\"","zh":"「開春一個月了，我沒覺著。我這冷法，像旁人臘月裡那樣。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Now feel the pulse at the chi position and press hard. Tell me at what depth you find it.\"","zh":"「今按其尺，重取之。且言於何位始得。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Cold from the root, a heart that flutters, and water gathering at the lowest point. Say how those three are one thing.\"","zh":"「本寒、心悸、水聚於下。且言此三者何以為一。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"cold_heat","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"excess_def","dx":"channel_organ","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"cold_heat"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Water and Fire in Mutual Aid","cardZh":"心腎陽虛 · 水火既濟","cardTxt":"The Heart is fire and sits at the top; the Kidney is water and sits at the bottom. In health the fire descends to warm the water so it does not freeze, and the water rises to cool the fire so it does not scorch — 心腎相交, 水火既濟. Two ways for that circuit to fail, and they look nothing alike. When the water is short, the fire is no longer restrained and floats up: restlessness, insomnia, night sweats, a red peeled tongue, a thin rapid pulse — 心腎不交, and you fill the water. When the yang is short, the fire cannot get down to warm the water: aversion to cold, cold limbs, palpitations, a pale swollen wet tongue, a deep slow pulse — and you warm the fire from the bottom, at the gate of vitality, not from the top. There is a third stage worth recognising early. Kidney yang also drives qi transformation and moves water; when it fails, water is not moved, it pools at the lowest point, and if it rises to the chest it presses on the Heart itself — 水氣凌心: palpitations that worsen when lying down, breathlessness, swelling that climbs. That progression is the reason the safety screen in this chapter comes before the pattern and not after it.","herbId":"rougui","herbEn":"Cinnamon Bark","herbZh":"肉桂","herbImg":"art/card-rougui.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Acrid, sweet and very hot, entering Kidney, Spleen, Heart and Liver. It supplements the fire of the gate of vitality, warms the channels and disperses cold, stops cold pain, and leads floating fire back down to its source. Note which part of the tree it is: Guizhi is the twig and releases the exterior, Rougui is the trunk bark and warms the interior. Very hot and dispersing, so it is contraindicated in yin deficiency with heat, in active bleeding, and in pregnancy."},"endings":{"three":["Six weeks on his hands are warm at the end of a night shift, the swelling is gone by morning instead of lasting all day, and the fluttering comes maybe once a week.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You warmed the bottom, not the top. Anyone can see that a cold man needs warming; knowing <i>where</i> to put the fire is the part that took you twenty-four chapters.\"","六週之後，一夜巡更下來手仍是溫的；腫至天明即消，不復終日；心中悸動，約旬日一二次。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你溫其下而不溫其上。人寒當溫，此誰不知；難在知火當置於<b>何處</b>——此汝二十四章之所學也。」"],"two":["He is warmer. The ankles still swell by evening.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You warmed him. Warming and moving water are two jobs, and the second one has a mechanism you have not named yet.\"","身已溫，而暮則足踝猶腫。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你溫之矣。溫與行水，二事也；其第二事之機轉，你尚未名之。」"],"one":["No change, and he says he felt hot in the face for a day and then cold again.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Then you put the fire at the top. Heat that rises and leaves is heat that never reached the root. Go and read what 引火歸元 means, and why it is a small dose.\"","無所改，且言面熱一日而復寒。<br><b>參師父：</b>「是置火於上也。升而即散之熱，未嘗及其根。且去讀『引火歸元』之義，並思其何以宜少量。」"],"titles":["Uncle Cui Feels the Spring","Uncle Cui Wears One Coat Fewer","Uncle Cui Waits for Summer"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Palpitations, swelling and breathlessness together. Screen him first — that combination is the one you never wave through.","cn":"心悸、浮腫、氣促並見。先做篩查——此組合斷不可輕放。"},{"w":"patient","en":"I walk the streets from dusk to dawn with the clapper. Thirty-two years.","cn":"我打更，從黃昏走到天亮，三十二年了。"},{"w":"patient","en":"My hands and feet are cold all night and they do not warm up when I get home. My knees and my back ache and feel weak.","cn":"整夜手足冰冷，到家也暖不過來。腰膝痠軟無力。"},{"w":"patient","en":"And my heart flutters when I climb the bridge. By evening my ankles are swollen over the tops of my shoes.","cn":"上橋時心裡就撲通撲通。到了晚上，足踝腫得漫過鞋幫。"},{"w":"master","en":"Cold at the root, a fluttering heart, water at the lowest point. Say how one shortage produces all three.","cn":"本寒、心悸、水聚於下。且言一虛何以生此三者。"}],"qa":[{"q":"Are you cold all over, or only in the hands and feet?","cq":"通身俱寒？抑但手足冷？","good":1,"a":"All over. But the hands and feet are the worst — cold to the wrist and the ankle, and they stay cold.","ca":"通身。手足尤甚——冷至腕踝，且久不回溫。","clue":{"en":"Whole-body cold with cold extremities to wrist and ankle","zh":"通身畏寒，四肢厥冷至腕踝"},"note":"Two different findings and both matter. <b>Aversion to cold that a warm room does not fix</b> 畏寒 is yang deficiency; contrast it with <b>aversion to cold in a new illness</b> 惡寒, which comes with fever and a floating pulse and passes in days. And <b>cold extremities</b> tell you how far the yang reaches — the yang warms the body from the trunk outward, so when it is short, the ends go first and the coldness climbs. How far up it has climbed is a rough measure of how deep the deficiency runs. 二證各有所指。<b>畏寒</b>而近火加衣不解者，陽虛也；當別於新病之<b>惡寒</b>——彼兼發熱、脈浮，數日而已。<b>四肢厥冷</b>者，可測陽氣所及之遠近：陽自中而達於四末，陽衰則末先冷，而寒自末上行。其上行之高下，即其虛之深淺之約數也。"},{"q":"When do the palpitations come, and what are you doing?","cq":"悸作於何時？其時方為何事？","good":1,"a":"When I climb the bridge, or the stairs. It settles if I stop and stand still.","ca":"上橋、上樓時。停下站定便平。","clue":{"en":"Palpitations on exertion, settling with rest","zh":"勞則心悸，息則自平"},"note":"Worse on exertion and better with rest is the deficiency signature again, and it is worth being explicit about what it rules out. Palpitations from phlegm-fire come with irritability, a bitter mouth, a greasy yellow coat and a slippery rapid pulse, and they do not care whether the patient is resting. Palpitations from blood stasis come with a stabbing chest pain and a purple tongue. His arrive with effort and leave with stillness, which is the answer of an engine that is underpowered rather than obstructed. 動則甚、靜則減，虛證之定式也，而其所排除者尤宜明言。痰火之悸，兼煩躁、口苦、苔黃膩、脈滑數，且不隨勞逸而異。血瘀之悸，兼胸痛如刺、舌紫。今其悸因勞而作、得靜而平——此力不足之答，非有物阻之答。"},{"q":"Tell me about the swelling. When is it worst, and does it leave a dent when pressed?","cq":"其腫何時最甚？按之留痕否？","good":1,"a":"Worst by evening, both ankles the same. Press it and the dent stays a while. By morning it has gone down.","ca":"暮時最甚，兩踝相等。按之凹陷，久乃復。晨起則消。","clue":{"en":"Symmetrical pitting ankle oedema, worse by evening, better by morning","zh":"兩踝對稱凹陷性浮腫，暮甚朝輕"},"note":"Three details, each doing work. <b>Both ankles equally</b> makes it systemic rather than a problem in one leg. <b>Worse by evening, better by morning</b> is water obeying gravity through the day and redistributing when he lies down — which also tells you the water is mobile rather than fixed. <b>Pitting</b> confirms it is fluid. Mechanically: Kidney yang drives qi transformation 氣化, and qi transformation is what moves water; when the yang is short the water is not moved and settles at the lowest point. Swelling here is not a separate illness, it is the same shortage seen from below. 三事各有其用。<b>兩踝相等</b>者，其病在身而不在一腿。<b>暮甚朝輕</b>者，水隨地而下，臥則復散——且知其水尚能行而未成堅積。<b>按之凹陷</b>者，證其為水。其機曰：腎陽主氣化，氣化者所以行水；陽衰則水不得行而聚於最下。故其腫非別為一病，乃同一虛而自下觀之耳。"},{"q":"How is your urine, and do you get up at night?","cq":"小便何如？夜起否？","good":1,"a":"Clear and a lot of it, especially at night. Three or four times, and it is pale as water.","ca":"清而多，夜間尤甚，三四次，色淡如水。","clue":{"en":"Copious clear urine, frequent at night","zh":"小便清長，夜尿頻多"},"note":"Read this beside the swelling, because at first glance the two contradict each other — how can a man retain water and pass a great deal of it? <b>Clear and copious</b> is the signature of cold: there is no heat to concentrate it, so it comes out pale and plentiful, and nocturia specifically points at the Kidney. The water that pools in his ankles is water that qi transformation never distributed properly to begin with; volume passed and water correctly moved are different things. When two findings seem to contradict, that is usually where the mechanism is hiding. 此當與其腫並讀，蓋乍看似相牴牾：水既留而何以復多溲？<b>清長</b>者寒之候：無熱以灼之，故色淡而量多；而夜尿頻多，尤指於腎。其踝間所聚者，本氣化所未嘗布散之水；溲之量與水之得行，二事也。凡二證似相反者，其機每藏於其間。"},{"q":"Is your face pale, or grey, or flushed at any time?","cq":"面色㿠白？晦暗？抑或時或潮紅？","good":1,"a":"White, my wife says. Never red.","ca":"內人說是白的。從不發紅。","clue":{"en":"Pale white complexion, never flushed","zh":"面色㿠白，無潮紅"},"note":"Asked for a specific reason. In deep yang deficiency the fire can be driven upward out of a cold root, and the patient shows a flushed face on a cold body — 真寒假熱, true cold with a false heat sign, and it is the presentation that gets misread and treated with cooling herbs. He has no flush, so the picture is straightforwardly cold. But you must ask, because the exception looks exactly like its opposite. 此問有故。陽虛之極，虛陽可為下寒所迫而上浮，則見面赤而身反冷——是為<b>真寒假熱</b>，最易誤認，而誤投寒涼者多在於此。今其面無潮紅，故其證為純寒。然必問之，蓋其變者，望之適如其反。"},{"q":"Have you had this every winter, or is this year different?","cq":"歷年冬日皆然？抑今歲獨異？","good":1,"a":"Every winter it was bad and every spring it lifted. This year spring came and it did not lift.","ca":"往年冬日亦苦，入春即解。今年春已至，而不解。","clue":{"en":"Long-standing cold intolerance that no longer lifts with the season","zh":"素畏寒，今春不復自解"},"note":"The question that dates the illness against something outside the patient. A long slow deficiency that used to recover with the warm season and now does not has crossed a line: the body was borrowing warmth from the summer to make up its shortfall, and the shortfall has outgrown what the season can lend. It also gives you a plain measure of success that he will notice himself — whether next spring lifts it. 此問以身外之候紀其病。素虛而向能借夏令之溫以自濟者，今不復濟，則已越一界：其所虧者，已過時令所能貸之數。且與病人一可自驗之準——來春能解與否。"}],"look":[{"t":"Pale and swollen with tooth marks, white coat, visibly wet","c":"舌淡胖有齒痕，苔白，望之濕潤","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Pale swollen toothmarked tongue, white wet coat","zh":"舌淡胖有齒痕，苔白滑"},"note":"Correct, and every feature is the same statement. <b>Pale</b> — not enough warmth and not enough blood reaching the tongue. <b>Swollen with tooth marks</b> — the tongue is waterlogged and presses against the teeth, because qi and yang are not transforming fluid. <b>White</b> — cold, not heat. <b>Wet</b> — water standing on the surface, and this is the feature that separates yang deficiency from plain qi deficiency: qi deficiency gives a pale tongue that is normally moist, while yang deficiency gives one that is visibly wet, because cold does not move water. Look at the shine, not only the colour. 是，而諸候同出一語。<b>淡</b>者，溫與血俱不上榮。<b>胖而有齒痕</b>者，舌為水所浸而擠於齒，氣陽不化津故也。<b>白</b>者寒。<b>滑</b>者水停舌面——此正別陽虛於單氣虛之處：氣虛者舌淡而潤如常，陽虛者舌淡而<b>濕</b>，蓋寒不行水也。當觀其光，不獨觀其色。"},{"t":"Pale and thin, dry, with a thin coat","c":"舌淡瘦而乾，苔薄","ok":0,"note":"Blood deficiency, or blood and essence together — that is the copyist, two chapters ago. Pale but <i>thin and dry</i> rather than swollen and wet. The colour agrees; the shape and the moisture do not. 血虛，或精血兩虧——即前二章之抄書人。同為舌淡，而彼<b>瘦而乾</b>，此胖而濕。其色雖同，形與潤則異。"},{"t":"Red with a peeled coat","c":"舌紅苔剝","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat, and the exact opposite half of the same organ. Kidney yin depletion and Kidney yang depletion are both Kidney depletion; the tongue is where they separate at a glance. 陰虛內熱也，與此同臟而異其半。腎陰虛、腎陽虛，俱為腎虛；一望其舌，而二者判然。"},{"t":"Purple with distended sublingual veins","c":"舌紫，舌下絡脈怒張","ok":0,"note":"Blood stasis, and in a heart case it is a reading to look for deliberately — prolonged yang deficiency does eventually fail to move blood, and stasis follows cold. Watch for it at every visit. It has not happened yet. 血瘀也。心病者當專察之：陽虛既久，終不能行血，寒久必瘀。逐診宜察。今其舌未至。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Deep, slow and thin 沉遲細","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Deep slow thin pulse","zh":"脈沉遲而細"},"note":"Correct, and three qualities give you three separate pieces of information. <b>Deep</b> 沉 — found only on heavy pressure — says the disorder is interior, not on the surface. <b>Slow</b> 遲, under four beats to a breath, says cold. <b>Thin</b> 細 says insufficiency. Interior, cold, deficient: that is yang deficiency spelled out in three characters, and it is why the pulse is worth taking slowly at all three depths rather than reporting one word. Compare an interior cold <i>excess</i> — cold congealing rather than yang failing — which is deep and slow but <b>tight and forceful</b>. Force is the discriminator, as it so often is. 是，三象而得三事。<b>沉</b>者重按始得，主病在裡而不在表。<b>遲</b>者一息不及四至，主寒。<b>細</b>者主不足。裡、寒、虛三字，即陽虛之全解——此所以診脈當緩取三候，而不徒以一字報之。試較之裡寒<b>實</b>證（寒凝而非陽衰）：其脈亦沉亦遲，而<b>緊而有力</b>。決之者仍在有力無力。"},{"t":"Deep, slow and tight with force 沉遲緊而有力","ok":0,"note":"Interior cold excess — cold has congealed and the body still has strength to fight it, as in acute cold abdominal pain. The treatment there is to warm and <i>disperse</i>; here it is to warm and <i>supplement</i>. One word of difference at the wrist, a different half of the pharmacy. 裡寒實證：寒凝而正氣尚能與之相搏，如暴受寒而腹痛者。彼當溫而<b>散</b>之，此當溫而<b>補</b>之。寸口一字之差，而所取之藥兩途。"},{"t":"Knotted or intermittent 結代","ok":0,"note":"Not what he has today — but this is the pulse to check for at every single visit in this case, and to count when you find it. A pausing pulse in a patient with palpitations and oedema changes the urgency of everything. Record the number so next week&#39;s reading means something. 今日非是——然本案逐診必察此脈，得之則當計其至數。心悸浮腫而脈見歇止者，其緩急全異。記其數，則他日之診有所比。"},{"t":"Thin and rapid 細數","ok":0,"note":"Thin agrees; rapid is the opposite of what your finger is telling you. That is the yin-deficient pulse from the previous chapter — same organ, other half, opposite temperature. 細者同，數則與指下所得適相反。此前章陰虛之脈：同臟異半，寒熱相反。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — he is cold and his heart flutters. Is this the Heart alone, or the Heart with something below it?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：其人寒而心悸。病獨在心？抑心兼其下者？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Heart and Kidney together — the palpitations are the Heart, but the aversion to cold, weak back and knees, nocturia and a deep chi pulse are all below","c":"心腎同病 — 悸屬心，而畏寒、腰膝痠軟、夜尿、尺脈沉，皆在其下","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and the evidence divides cleanly. <b>The Heart&#39;s half</b>: palpitations on exertion, a pale complexion — the Heart governs the blood and the vessels and the yang of the chest drives them. <b>The Kidney&#39;s half</b>: aversion to cold that a warm room does not fix, cold limbs, weak sore back and knees, copious clear urine with nocturia, a deep weak chi pulse — bones, low back, water and the deepest reserve of yang all report to the Kidney. Two organs, one shortage of yang, and the reason they fail together is the next question. 是，其據自分。<b>屬心者</b>：勞則心悸、面色㿠白——心主血脈，而胸中之陽鼓之。<b>屬腎者</b>：畏寒而近火不解、四肢厥冷、腰膝痠軟、小便清長而夜尿頻、尺脈沉弱——骨、腰、水，與陽氣之根，皆屬於腎。二臟一陽虛，而其所以並衰者，即下一問。"},{"t":"The Heart alone","c":"獨病在心","ok":0,"note":"It would explain the palpitations and nothing else. Weak knees, nocturia, whole-body cold and a chi pulse you cannot find are not Heart findings, and a diagnosis that leaves four findings homeless is half a diagnosis. 但可解其悸，餘皆不可解。腰膝、夜尿、通身之寒、尺脈難尋，皆非心之候；有四證無所歸者，其診止得其半。"},{"t":"The Spleen — his limbs are cold and he is swollen","c":"病在脾 — 肢冷而腫","ok":0,"note":"The Spleen is involved: Spleen yang deficiency also gives cold limbs and oedema, and in practice Spleen and Kidney yang usually fail together. But the Spleen&#39;s own picture is loose stools, abdominal distension after eating, poor appetite and heaviness, and he reports none of those. And it is the Kidney, not the Spleen, that holds the root fire the Spleen itself depends on. 脾誠有涉：脾陽虛亦見肢冷浮腫，且臨證脾腎之陽多同衰。然脾之本證為便溏、食後腹脹、納呆、身重，其人皆無。且藏根火而為脾所賴者，腎也，非脾也。"},{"t":"The Lung — he is breathless on the bridge","c":"病在肺 — 登橋而喘","ok":0,"note":"Breathlessness has many sources. His arrives together with the palpitations, on exertion, in a man whose ankles swell — that is a circulation of yang failing, not a Lung failing to descend qi. And the safety screen has already asked the question that would matter if it were the Lung. 喘之所自者多。今其喘與悸同來、因勞而作，且其踝腫——此陽氣運行之衰，非肺失肅降。且若在肺，其所當問者，篩查已問之矣。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — the Heart is fire above and the Kidney is water below. What has broken between them?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：心火在上，腎水在下。二者之間，所壞者何？</small>","opts":[{"t":"The fire cannot descend to warm the water — the yang is short, so the circuit fails from the bottom","c":"火不下溫其水 — 陽氣既衰，其交自下而斷","ok":1,"note":"Correct. In health the Heart fire descends to warm the Kidney water so it does not freeze, and the Kidney water rises to cool the Heart fire so it does not scorch — 心腎相交, 水火既濟. Here the yang itself is short, so there is not enough fire to send downward: the water below is unwarmed and does not move, and it pools at the lowest point of the body. Note carefully that this is <i>not</i> the more familiar 心腎不交 of insomnia, where the <b>water</b> is short and the unrestrained fire floats up — that patient is restless, sleepless, sweating at night, red-tongued and fast-pulsed. Same axis, opposite end, opposite treatment. Both are called a failure of Heart and Kidney to communicate, and telling them apart takes one look at the tongue. 是。平人則心火下溫腎水，使不寒；腎水上濟心火，使不亢——心腎相交，水火既濟。今陽氣自虛，無火可下：水失其溫而不行，聚於身之最下。當細辨者：此<b>非</b>寐證所常言之心腎不交——彼者<b>水</b>虧而火失所制，浮越於上，其人煩而不寐、盜汗、舌紅、脈數。同一軸而異其端，其治相反。二者俱名心腎不交，而別之者，一望其舌足矣。"},{"t":"The water cannot rise to cool the fire — the yin is short","c":"水不上濟其火 — 陰虛","ok":0,"note":"That is the other end of the same axis, and it is the one most students name first because it is the one in the insomnia chapters. Check it against him: he is not restless, not sleepless, not sweating at night; his tongue is pale, swollen and wet, and his pulse is slow. Every finding is the opposite. 此同軸之另端，學者每先舉之，以其常見於不寐諸章故也。試以其人核之：不煩、不失眠、無盜汗；舌淡胖而滑，脈遲。無一不反。"},{"t":"Nothing is broken between them; they are two separate illnesses","c":"二者無所相干，各自為病","ok":0,"note":"Then you would need two mechanisms for one shortage that produces cold at the ends, weakness at the root, fluttering at the top and water at the bottom — all of which resolve together when the yang is warmed. One explanation that covers everything beats two that each cover half. 若然，則一虛而生四證——末寒、本弱、上悸、下水——須以二機解之；而溫其陽則四者同愈。一說而盡之者，勝於二說而各得其半。"},{"t":"The Heart fire is excessive and burning the water away","c":"心火亢盛，灼其水","ok":0,"note":"That patient is hot, red-faced, restless, thirsty, with mouth ulcers, dark urine and a rapid forceful pulse. This one keeps his hands in his sleeves in a warm room. 彼者身熱面赤、煩躁、口渴、口瘡、溲赤，脈數有力。此人於溫室之中猶袖其手。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — the water is at his ankles today. Where does this pattern go if it is not treated, and what would tell you it had gone there?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：今其水在踝。此證不治則傳於何？何以知其已傳？</small>","opts":[{"t":"水氣凌心 — the water climbs and presses on the Heart: palpitations that worsen lying down, breathlessness that forces him to sit up, swelling rising from ankles to legs to abdomen","c":"水氣凌心 — 水氣上逆迫心：臥則悸甚、不得平臥、腫自踝而上及腿腹","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and knowing the destination is what makes the safety screen in this chapter meaningful rather than ritual. If the yang keeps failing, qi transformation keeps failing, water keeps accumulating and it does not stay at the ankles — it climbs, and when it reaches the chest it presses on the Heart itself: 水氣凌心. The signs to watch for, and to re-ask at every visit, are precisely the ones the screen asked at the start: <b>palpitations that get worse rather than better on lying down</b>, <b>breathlessness that forces him to prop himself up at night</b>, <b>swelling that has climbed above the ankle</b>, and <b>a pulse that begins to pause</b>. Any of those and the answer is not a stronger prescription — it is a physician, promptly, alongside whatever you are doing. Tell the patient which changes to report, in his own words, before he leaves. 是。知其所往，則本章之篩查非為儀節而有其實。陽衰不已，則氣化不行，水積不止，且不止於踝——其水上行，及胸則迫心，是謂<b>水氣凌心</b>。當察而逐診再問者，正篩查所首問之數事：<b>臥則悸反甚</b>、<b>夜不得平臥而須端坐以息</b>、<b>腫已過踝而上</b>、<b>脈始見歇止</b>。有其一者，所當為非增其方之力，乃即令就醫，而所治不廢。且當於其去前，以其能記之語，明告何者當來報。"},{"t":"It becomes yin deficiency in time","c":"久則轉為陰虛","ok":0,"note":"Long yang deficiency can eventually injure yin — nothing in the body stays on one side forever — but that is a slow late complication, not the near destination. The question asks what to watch for next month, and the answer is the water. 陽虛既久，誠可及陰——身中之事，無久居一偏者。然此為遲而後至之變，非其近路。所問者，來月所當察者為何；其答在水。"},{"t":"It stays where it is; ankle swelling in an old man is simply age","c":"止於其處。老人踝腫，年事而已","ok":0,"note":"Age explains why he is vulnerable, not what is happening or where it goes. And a pattern that has already broken through a season it used to recover in is a pattern that is moving. 年高者，言其所以易受，非言其所患與所往。且素能隨春而解，今不解矣——是其病方行，非其病已定。"},{"t":"Toward blood stasis, and nothing else","c":"惟傳為血瘀，別無他變","ok":0,"note":"Blood stasis is a real and common late development — cold congeals, and yang that cannot move blood eventually lets it stall, which is why the sublingual veins are worth checking. But naming it as the <i>only</i> road misses the one that arrives sooner and matters more urgently. 血瘀誠為後起之常變：寒主凝，陽不行血則終致其滯，故舌下絡脈當察。然謂其<b>惟</b>此一路者，則遺其至之較速而急者。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"KI3","t":"T&#224;ix&#299; KI3 太谿","ok":1,"note":"The Source point of the Kidney, needled with reinforcing method and moxa. You have used this point before to enrich Kidney yin; today the same point is warmed for Kidney yang, and that is worth pausing on — a Source point is where the original qi of its organ surfaces, so it supplements whichever half of that organ is short. The point does not change; the technique and the intention do. 腎之原穴，用補法而加灸。前此取之以滋腎陰，今則溫之以助腎陽——此一節宜留意：原穴者，臟之原氣所發，故隨其臟之所虧而補之。穴不易，而其法與其意易之。"},{"id":"CV4","t":"Gu&#257;ny&#225;n CV4 關元","ok":1,"note":"On the midline, three cun below the navel: the Front-Mu point of the Small Intestine, a meeting point of the three leg yin channels with the Ren mai, and by long tradition the place where original qi is stored and where the yang of the whole body is warmed. This is the classical site for moxa in yang depletion — generous, repeated, over weeks. If you warm one point in this case, warm this one. 在臍下三寸正中：小腸之募穴，足三陰與任脈之會，而古來以為元氣所藏、一身之陽所溫之處。陽虛用灸，此為古法首選——宜多壯、宜屢施、宜以旬月計。此案若但灸一穴，則灸此。"},{"id":"BL23","t":"Sh&#232;nsh&#363; BL23 腎俞","ok":1,"note":"The Back-Shu point of the Kidney, level with the second lumbar vertebra. Back-Shu points are where an organ&#39;s qi infuses at the back, and pairing a Back-Shu with a Front-Mu — BL23 with CV4 here — is one of the oldest and most reliable ways to treat an organ from both sides at once. It also sits exactly where his back aches. 腎之背俞穴，在第二腰椎之旁。背俞者，臟氣輸注於背之處；俞募相配——今以腎俞配關元——為古法之最可恃者，前後夾治其臟。且其位正當其腰痠之所。"},{"id":"KI2","t":"R&#225;ng&#468; KI2 然谷","ok":0,"note":"The Spring point of the Kidney, used to clear heat from the Kidney channel and to settle empty fire — mouth and throat heat, night sweats, a red tongue. This patient has no heat at all, and clearing him would take away what little warmth he has. 腎之滎穴，主清腎經之熱、降虛火：口咽熱、盜汗、舌紅。今其人通身無熱，清之則奪其僅存之溫。"},{"id":"LU5","t":"Ch&#464;z&#233; LU5 尺澤","ok":0,"note":"The Sea point of the Lung, for clearing Lung heat and descending rebellious qi in a full cough. He is breathless on exertion, not coughing, and nothing in this case is full or hot. 肺之合穴，主清肺熱、降逆氣，用於實咳。今其人因勞而喘而不咳，且通案無實無熱。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Y&#299;nl&#237;ngqu&#225;n SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"The tempting wrong answer, because there is visible water and this is the damp-draining point. But draining water in a patient whose problem is that he has no yang to move it treats the puddle and ignores the pump — the water comes back, and he is weaker. Restore qi transformation by warming the yang, and the water moves itself. If you want a point that moves water in a cold pattern, warm the Kidney rather than drain the Spleen. 此誤最誘人：目見有水，而此為利濕之穴。然其病在無陽以行水，徒利其水者，治其潦而遺其樞——水必復聚，而其人益虛。溫其陽以復氣化，則水自行。若必欲取行水之穴，當溫其腎，不當瀉其脾。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method with generous moxa, warming from below","c":"補法，重灸，溫自下起","ok":1,"note":"<b>Correct, and this is the case moxa exists for.</b> Reinforcing, because everything is empty. Generous moxa, because the pattern is yang deficiency with no heat anywhere to forbid it — this is the one pattern family where warmth is not merely permitted but is the main treatment, and a timid amount of it does nothing. And warming <i>from below</i>: the fire has to be replaced at the root, at CV4 and the Kidney points, not at the chest where the symptom is loudest. Compare the last chapter, where moxa was forbidden outright for a patient who looked equally unwell — the technique follows the pattern, and the two patterns were opposite halves of the same organ. 是，艾灸之設，正為此案。補者，通身皆虛。重灸者，其證為陽虛而通身無熱以禁之——諸證之中，惟此一家，溫非特可用，且為其主治；而灸而畏其多者，等於未灸。溫自下起者：火當復於其根，在關元與腎家諸穴，不在胸中證之最著處。試較前章：其人望之同為困憊，而灸為所絕禁——法隨證轉，而二證正一臟之兩半也。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, but no moxa in an elderly patient","c":"補法，然年高者不宜灸","ok":0,"note":"Age is not a contraindication to moxa; heat is, and dryness is, and thin or numb skin needs care in the technique. An older patient with genuine yang deficiency is close to the ideal candidate. Adjust how you moxa — indirect, watched, never to blistering, and check the skin because sensation may be reduced — but do not withhold the treatment the pattern is asking for. 年高非灸之禁；所禁者熱與燥，而膚薄或感覺遲鈍者，當謹其法。老年而實屬陽虛者，正灸之所宜。當調其法——隔物而灸、時時察之、不令起泡，且以其膚覺或減而屢視之——而不當廢其證之所求。"},{"t":"Reducing method to move the water out","c":"瀉法以逐其水","ok":0,"note":"The water is a consequence, not the pathogen. Reducing a man whose pulse you can barely find takes away the yang that was supposed to move the water, and he swells further within days. In a deficiency pattern with accumulation, restore the function first; the accumulation follows. 水者其果，非其邪也。脈且難尋而復瀉之，是奪其行水之陽，數日而腫益甚。凡虛中有積者，先復其用，則積自去。"},{"t":"Even method, since there is both deficiency and accumulated water","c":"平補平瀉，以其虛中有水故","ok":0,"note":"The most thoughtful wrong answer, and worth taking seriously — this genuinely is deficiency with an accumulation, which is where even method usually belongs. But the accumulation here is not a pathogen that arrived from outside; it is the direct product of the deficiency, and it resolves when the deficiency does. Supplement and warm, hold the reducing, and watch the ankles as your measure. 此誤最有思致，宜為詳辨——本案誠屬虛中夾積，而平法所主，正在於此。然其積非外來之邪，乃虛之所自生，虛復則積自消。故當補而溫之，瀉法且置，而以其踝為驗效之準。"}]};
